users/ScriptedAlchemy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ScriptedAlchemy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ScriptedAlchemy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ScriptedAlchemy","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/rsbuild-plugin-react-router/commits/2b04e536ce02ba0c6668fdb6ceebe78660dd2587/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T22:36:49Z","email":"25274700+ScriptedAlchemy@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Zack Jackson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T22:36:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(federation): startup and export propagation through MF async startup; RSC edge cases (#134)\n\nFixes #132. Browser route-module entries are made async so Rspack awaits the MF startup before exporting; federation containers get their own runtime chunk; server code splitting is async-only under federation (enforced at the final tools.rspack boundary, incl. cache groups) so @module-federation/node''s chunk loader satisfies the server build''s startup. asyncStartup stays enforced everywhere; sharing stays non-eager. RSC: manifest alignment handles an empty browser assetPrefix; filename validation uses emitted chunk metadata. Federation example CORS scoped to asset handlers.","tree":{"sha":"c4cc1adedb3932ead20f2048f325f59ed7509bd6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/rsbuild-plugin-react-router/git/trees/c4cc1adedb3932ead20f2048f325f59ed7509bd6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rstackjs/rsbuild-plugin-react-router/git/commits/2b04e536ce02ba0c6668fdb6ceebe78660dd2587","verification":{"payload":"tree c4cc1adedb3932ead20f2048f325f59ed7509bd6\nparent c0dc8e29660448c21852eb0f74d8cfd2a8c43994\nauthor Zack Jackson <25274700+ScriptedAlchemy@users.noreply.github.com> 1789079809 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789079809 -0700\n\nfix(federation): startup and export 