dDate":"2026-09-30T11:58:02Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"yahyafakhroji","providerType":"User"},"email":"yahya.fakhroji@gmail.com","name":"Yahya Fakhroji"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T18:42:18.071Z","repositoryId":926358834,"sha":"64aba84228d44fcf3f0986bc4799242667ea36fb"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"yahyafakhroji","providerType":"User"},"email":"yahya.fakhroji@gmail.com","name":"Yahya Fakhroji"},"authoredDate":"2026-09-30T11:43:45Z","committedDate":"2026-09-30T11:43:45Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"yahyafakhroji","providerType":"User"},"email":"yahya.fakhroji@gmail.com","name":"Yahya Fakhroji"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T18:42:18.071Z","repositoryId":926358834,"sha":"e8cd20989bb7085d1b7032722263aebca92cab19"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"yahyafakhroji","providerType":"User"},"email":"yahya.fakhroji@gmail.com","name":"Yahya Fakhroji"},"authoredDate":"2026-09-30T11:31:43Z","committedDate":"2026-09-30T11:31:43Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"yahyafakhroji","providerType":"User"},"email":"yahya.fakhroji@gmail.com","name":"Yahya Fakhroji"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T18:42:18.071Z","repositoryId":926358834,"sha":"8cc1a888795b177f5104f1fa7006e0801eda3c11"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"yahyafakhroji","providerType":"User"},"email":"yahya.fakhroji@gmail.com","name":"Yahya Fakhroji"},"authoredDate":"2026-09-30T11:31:39Z","committedDate":"2026-09-30T11:31:39Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"yahyafakhroji","providerType":"User"},"email":"yahya.fakhroji@gmail.com","name":"Yahya Fakhroji"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T18:42:18.071Z","repositoryId":926358834,"sha":"7ff26a0dc993cadea95725fb1a133462f511a7c1"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"yahyafakhroji","providerType":"User"},"email":"yahya.fakhroji@gmail.com","name":"Yahya Fakhroji"},"authoredDate":"2026-09-30T11:31:33Z","committedDate":"2026-09-30T11:31:33Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"yahyafakhroji","providerType":"User"},"email":"yahya.fakhroji@gmail.com","name":"Yahya Fakhroji"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T18:42:18.071Z","repositoryId":926358834,"sha":"a62a028f20101aa7882bd2d8435d747f18530b43"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"mattdjenkinson","providerType":"User"},"email":"75292329+mattdjenkinson@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Matt Jenkinson"},"authoredDate":"2026-09-30T10:22:55Z","committedDate":"2026-09-30T10:22:55Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T18:42:18.071Z","repositoryId":926358834,"sha":"15557327e2450e5016a5011e023c422a72a520f6"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"yahyafakhroji","providerType":"User"},"email":"yahya.fakhroji@gmail.com","name":"Yahya Fakhroji"},"authoredDate":"2026-09-30T10:13:04Z","committedDate":"2026-09-30T10:13:04Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T18:42:18.071Z","repositoryId":926358834,"sha":"35b8ae310348a5ba82a7242d733b55006d6af9e4"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"yahyafakhroji","providerType":"User"},"email":"yahya.fakhroji@gmail.com","name":"Yahya Fakhroji"},"authoredDate":"2026-09-30T10:10:34Z","committedDate":"2026-09-30T10:10:34Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T18:42:18.071Z","repositoryId":926358834,"sha":"88cfaca4e0b155d9439048923268658c2313f9a8"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-08T18:42:18.071Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75292329?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mattdjenkinson","id":75292329,"login":"mattdjenkinson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MjkyMzI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commits/5f4d0b92128ec1041e1645bb65db965517cf2a06/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T13:03:12Z","email":"75292329+mattdjenkinson@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Matt Jenkinson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T13:03:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(edge): only allow verified domains as ALB hostnames (#1653)\n\nAdding a hostname on an unverified domain to an Application Load\nBalancer leaves the proxy in Programming until the domain verifies, and\nit errors if the domain never does. The hostnames dialog let you pick an\nunverified domain, or type any hostname at all, so it was easy to leave\na load balancer stuck. Now only verified domains can be used.\n\n| | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| Unverified domain in the picker | selectable, with an amber warning |\nlisted with its Unverified badge, not selectable |\n| \"Type a custom hostname\" | accepted any text | removed |\n| Saving a new hostname on an unverified domain | saved, proxy stuck in\nProgramming | blocked, with \"example.com isn''t verified yet\" on the row\n|\n| New wildcard whose domain isn''t proven by DNS TXT record | saved with\nan amber warning, then refused by the operator | blocked, with the\nreason on the row |\n| Hostname already on the proxy, unverified | unchanged | kept with an\namber warning, so other edits still save |\n\n- A hostname counts as verified when any verified domain equals it or is\na parent of it. That''s the same rule the gateway controller in\nnetwork-services-operator uses, so `api.staging.example.com` is fine\nwhen `example.com` is verified.\n- Hostname rows now show their own errors. `Form.Field` only shows\nerrors for fields it marks touched, and a submit marks top-level keys\n(`hostnames`), never list rows (`hostnames[0]`), so a blocked save\nshowed nothing. This also brings back older row errors, like a hostname\nwith spaces in it.\n- Separate commit: the dialog now suggests hostnames for load balancers\nwithout a display name. `chosenName` is `''''` for proxies created outside\nthe portal, and `??` kept the empty string.\n\nThe `datumctl alb` side is datum-cloud/network-services-operator#570.\nNeither guard stops someone writing an `HTTPProxy` to the API directly.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nAn unverified domain is listed but can''t be picked.\n<img width=\"592\" height=\"372\" alt=\"1-unverified-domain-disabled\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4e936d38-a399-48bc-8fe5-0f34d2d69d89\"\n/>\n\nA hostname already on the proxy keeps its warning and doesn''t block\nsaving.\n<img width=\"592\" height=\"412\" alt=\"2-existing-hostname-warning\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b5687ebb-9ab5-4410-aa5e-61352e92f38e\"\n/>\n\nChanging it to a new hostname on that domain blocks Save, with the error\non the row.\n<img width=\"592\" height=\"448\" alt=\"3-new-unverified-blocked\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/618eb297-8e5a-4451-9cea-b80fb7138a82\"\n/>\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] Typecheck, lint, and unit tests for the verification rule pass\n- [x] On staging, `testing.com` (unverified) shows as Unverified and\ncan''t be selected; verified domains can\n- [x] On staging, an ALB with an existing `testing.com` hostname shows\nthe warning and still saves a new verified hostname next to it\n- [x] On staging, changing that row blocks Save with the error on the\nrow, and nothing reaches the API\n- [ ] An ALB created with `datumctl alb create` (no display name) gets\nname suggestions in the dialog\n\nPart of #1634","tree":{"sha":"bdf5f69720d66e585ccf693516923a5c02bae108","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/git/trees/bdf5f69720d66e585ccf693516923a5c02bae108"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/git/commits/5f4d0b92128ec1041e1645bb65db965517cf2a06","verification":{"payload":"tree bdf5f69720d66e585ccf693516923a5c02bae108\nparent b04d949f3fb4ffc5f1b8ffe10f5b0af110c6b42a\nparent b1e71d8cd9fed343f72e2fb200354790a9147e1e\nauthor Matt Jenkinson <75292329+mattdjenkinson@users.noreply.github.com> 1791464592 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791464592 +0100\n\nfix(edge): only allow verified domains as ALB hostnames (#1653)\n\nAdding a hostname on an unverified domain to an Application Load\nBalancer leaves the proxy in Programming until the domain verifies, and\nit errors if the domain never does. The hostnames dialog let you pick an\nunverified domain, or type any hostname at all, so it was easy to leave\na load balancer stuck. Now only verified domains can be used.\n\n| | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| Unverified domain in the picker | selectable, with an amber warning |\nlisted with its Unverified badge, not selectable |\n| \"Type a custom hostname\" | accepted any text | removed |\n| Saving a new hostname on an unverified domain | saved, proxy stuck in\nProgramming | blocked, with \"example.com isn''t verified yet\" on the row\n|\n| New wildcard whose domain isn''t proven by DNS TXT record | saved with\nan amber warning, then refused by the operator | blocked, with the\nreason on the row |\n| Hostname already on the proxy, unverified | unchanged | kept with an\namber warning, so other edits still save |\n\n- A hostname counts as verified when any verified domain equals it or is\na parent of it. That''s the same rule the gateway controller in\nnetwork-services-operator uses, so `api.staging.example.com` is fine\nwhen `example.com` is verified.\n- Hostname rows now show their own errors. `Form.Field` only shows\nerrors for fields it marks touched, and a submit marks top-level keys\n(`hostnames`), never list rows (`hostnames[0]`), so a blocked save\nshowed nothing. This also brings back older row errors, like a hostname\nwith spaces in it.\n- Separate commit: the dialog now suggests hostnames for load balancers\nwithout a display name. `chosenName` is `''''` for proxies created outside\nthe portal, and `??` kept the empty string.\n\nThe `datumctl alb` side is datum-cloud/network-services-operator#570.\nNeither guard stops someone writing an `HTTPProxy` to the API directly.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nAn unverified domain is listed but can''t be picked.\n<img width=\"592\" height=\"372\" alt=\"1-unverified-domain-disabled\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4e936d38-a399-48bc-8fe5-0f34d2d69d89\"\n/>\n\nA hostname already on the proxy keeps its warning and doesn''t block\nsaving.\n<img width=\"592\" height=\"412\" alt=\"2-existing-hostname-warning\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b5687ebb-9ab5-4410-aa5e-61352e92f38e\"\n/>\n\nChanging it to a new hostname on that domain blocks Save, with the error\non the row.\n<img width=\"592\" height=\"448\" alt=\"3-new-unverified-blocked\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/618eb297-8e5a-4451-9cea-b80fb7138a82\"\n/>\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] Typecheck, lint, and unit tests for the verification rule pass\n- [x] On staging, `testing.com` (unverified) shows as Unverified and\ncan''t be selected; verified domains can\n- [x] On staging, an ALB with an existing `testing.com` hostname shows\nthe warning and still saves a new verified hostname next to it\n- [x] On staging, changing that row blocks Save with the error on the\nrow, and nothing reaches the API\n- [ ] An ALB created with `datumctl alb create` (no display name) gets\nname suggestions in the dialog\n\nPart of #1634","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEG