tml_url":"https://github.com/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commit/abb51d2fd1b1e1a3378301899f09a099fd7046ce","sha":"abb51d2fd1b1e1a3378301899f09a099fd7046ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commits/abb51d2fd1b1e1a3378301899f09a099fd7046ce"}],"sha":"8377aaf26a2194508ee230cd14c979d567b36f79","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commits/8377aaf26a2194508ee230cd14c979d567b36f79"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75292329?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mattdjenkinson","id":75292329,"login":"mattdjenkinson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MjkyMzI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commits/abb51d2fd1b1e1a3378301899f09a099fd7046ce/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T13:51:01Z","email":"75292329+mattdjenkinson@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Matt Jenkinson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T13:51:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(watch): Keep other orgs'' projects out of the org projects list (#1640)\n\n**Problem**\nThe org projects list sometimes showed projects from other\norganizations. They flashed in, then disappeared on their own or after a\nrefresh. Milo''s org-scoped project watch wasn''t filtered by\norganization, so it streamed every org''s projects. Before #1633 the\nportal never applied ADDED events to the projects list, so this went\nunnoticed. Now that watch events write into the list, the replay sent on\neach subscribe added other orgs'' projects until the next REST refetch\nremoved them.\n\n**Solution**\nThe root cause is fixed in Milo in milo-os/milo#828. This PR is a\nbackstop so the portal never trusts the stream''s scoping by itself.\nWatch caches can now take an `accepts` check, and the project list watch\ndrops any project whose `organizationId` isn''t the org being viewed. I\ndeliberately didn''t make the watch apply the REST list''s Ready filter,\nbecause that would stop newly created projects showing while they\nprovision. A unit test covers another org''s ADDED being ignored and the\norg''s own projects still being added; it fails without the guard.","tree":{"sha":"f6a581857f2059f6f751ffd3b57df02a316b06ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/git/trees/f6a581857f2059f6f751ffd3b57df02a316b06ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/git/commits/abb51d2fd1b1e1a3378301899f09a099fd7046ce","verification":{"payload":"tree f6a581857f2059f6f751ffd3b57df02a316b06ae\nparent bb3c541c02cbd8a5550a92356fcd9d10a6605237\nparent c8744d78974042bbaf2c08ab34ae5e8840d12413\nauthor Matt Jenkinson <75292329+mattdjenkinson@users.noreply.github.com> 1791294661 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791294661 +0100\n\nfix(watch): Keep other orgs'' projects out of the org projects list (#1640)\n\n**Problem**\nThe org projects list sometimes showed projects from other\norganizations. They flashed in, then disappeared on their own or after a\nrefresh. Milo''s org-scoped project watch wasn''t filtered by\norganization, so it streamed every org''s projects. Before #1633 the\nportal never applied ADDED events to the projects list, so this went\nunnoticed. Now that watch events write into the list, the replay sent on\neach subscribe added other orgs'' projects until the next REST refetch\nremoved them.\n\n**Solution**\nThe root cause is fixed in Milo in milo-os/milo#828. This PR is a\nbackstop so the portal never trusts the stream''s scoping by itself.\nWatch caches can now take an `accepts` check, and the project list watch\ndrops any project whose `organizationId` isn''t the org being viewed. I\ndeliberately didn''t make the watch apply the REST list''s Ready filter,\nbecause that would stop newly created projects showing while they\nprovision. A unit test covers another org''s ADDED being ignored and the\norg''s own projects still being added; it fails without the guard.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxPzGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMLoQADrIXFDB1VZDY/qqLfZ7Kqhr\nxghHRH8Jv5xNLrNK+R2b0nMy6kT8Q4fBeez0MSTFkPzlkMtHAI7o2Ol/xRD3LjQ/\njjR8ID4j4dwOQKtg6P4zq733TWEJpqje3/ka8iGtLsfIiNal3g8hPBznE2R7XXvj\nBHGLU+rmrrvVm7I903PavvEuBWWHbP0GyG1QsrKt8oCQ5pl7Owj0x3U42M8ithUQ\na9hMmbmjlDYIbK4WNai883MWT1Jlhdc4PpnnmFAbL9vSaHNCg5radqj8YuHeIbbo\nUUyFv6fPZohcMDWwayEwdtrl1CC/KbKgCTxefjnsAe+LThqomHIUK4lEmMLts2QV\nk3rw0EHo+QWhtcqWzjRRPLaxaK7ZZVZL3CBMzfPbKh2CVhNs6wl3C5bMJEusp+77\nkLQZ6Zno9ngrfJEtImdirRM2FEf+47IdzEUv/n/F3eoA5YHjtSRN+3GmHO/qxCro\nLIjSuP6PlPSMpumOGaKMzWollCuSQNMsjL9URrNk4OlPn4+bm1kNkWlIpOsauBgs\nP2nyGt2OMPB87/TnTTHa8y4rMgcKmKCajEYur/nfhV+uj+7iPbXM7g6xivHhmXK4\nzBjXEhYw7BVuqWTtimMafpg9wu97TDlmtX8f7EDJmOJQdAywNDRXFjT7PSxw/iSa\neV7NT+FTXMr7NhbQNugW\n=c6iE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T13:51:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commit/abb51d2fd1b1e1a3378301899f09a099fd7046ce","node_id":"C_kwDONzcdMtoAKGFiYjUxZDJmZDFiMWUxYTMzNzgzMDE4OTlmMDlhMDk5ZmQ3MDQ2Y2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commit/bb3c541c02cbd8a5550a92356fcd9d10a6605237","sha":"bb3c541c02cbd8a5550a92356fcd9d10a6605237","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commits/bb3c541c02cbd8a5550a92356fcd9d10a6605237"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commit/c8744d78974042bbaf2c08ab34ae5e8840d12413","sha":"c8744d78974042bbaf2c08ab34ae5e8840d12413","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commits/c8744d78974042bbaf2c08ab34ae5e8840d12413"}],"sha":"abb51d2fd1b1e1a3378301899f09a099fd7046ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commits/abb51d2fd1b1e1a3378301899f09a099fd7046ce"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75292329?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mattdjenkinson","id":75292329,"login":"mattdjenkinson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MjkyMzI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commits/c8744d78974042bbaf2c08ab34ae5e8840d12413/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T13:44:21Z","email":"75292329+mattdjenkinson@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Matt Jenkinson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T13:44:21Z","email":"75292329+mattdjenkinson@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Matt Jenkinson"},"message":"fix(watch): keep other orgs'' projects out of the org projects list\n\nMilo''s org-scoped project watch was not filtered by organization, so it\nstreamed every org''s projects. Since the watch now writes ADDED events\ninto the org projects list, those projects flashed into the list until\nthe next refetch removed them.\n\nMilo is fixed in milo-os/milo#828. As a backstop, watch caches can now\ntake an `accepts` check, and the project list watch drops any project\nwhose organizationId is not the org being viewed.","tree":{"sha":"f6a581857f2059f6f751ffd3b57df02a316b06ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/git/trees/f6a581857f2059f6f751ffd3b57df02a316b06ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/git/commits/c8744d78974042bbaf2c08ab34ae5e8840d12413","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75292329?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mattdjenkinson","id":75292329,"login":"mattdjenkinson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MjkyMzI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commit/c8744d78974042bbaf2c08ab34ae5e8840d12413","node_id":"C_kwDONzcdMtoAKGM4NzQ0ZDc4OTc0MDQyYmJhZjJjMDhhYjM0YWU1ZTg4NDBkMTI0MTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commit/bb3c541c02cbd8a5550a92356fcd9d10a6605237","sha":"bb3c541c02cbd8a5550a92356fcd9d10a6605237","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commits/bb3c541c02cbd8a5550a92356fcd9d10a6605237"}],"sha":"c8744d78974042bbaf2c08ab34ae5e8840d12413","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commits/c8744d78974042bbaf2c08ab34ae5e8840d12413"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3510868?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahyafakhroji/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahyafakhroji/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahyafakhroji/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahyafakhroji/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yahyafakhroji","id":3510868,"login":"yahyafakhroji","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTA4Njg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahyafakhroji/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahyafakhroji/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahyafakhroji/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahyafakhroji/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahyafakhroji/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yahyafakhroji","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commits/bb3c541c02cbd8a5550a92356fcd9d10a6605237/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T12:13:54Z","email":"yahya.fakhroji@gmail.com","name":"Yahya Fakhroji"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T12:13:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(search): Show why project search failed instead of \"No matches\" (#1639)\n\n**Problem**\nWhen the project search request failed, the search bar and the mobile\nsearch sheet treated it as an empty result and showed \"No matches in\nthis project.\" A 403 from the search API looked exactly like a project\nwith nothing in it, so users concluded their resources were missing.\n\n**Solution**\nBoth surfaces now check the engine''s error state before the\nempty-results branch and show an error message instead. A 403 reads\n\"Search isn''t available for your account in this project.\" The wording\nis neutral on purpose, because project owners currently hit this through\na missing backend grant. Any other failure reads \"Search is temporarily\nunavailable.\" The screen-reader status text uses the same copy. Unit\ntests cover the 403, 500 and empty-error cases.\n\nRefs #1619","tree":{"sha":"e771f856d8532c14ae92147641cde2ffd51872d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/git/trees/e771f856d8532c14ae92147641cde2ffd51872d1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/git/commits/bb3c541c02cbd8a5550a92356fcd9d10a6605237","verification":{"payload":"tree e771f856d8532c14ae92147641cde2ffd51872d1\nparent d36b401e00f334adff29f90e8114cbb8b1e5abfd\nparent 20ed18283b10ea2a01e653603b8a7c93452b8283\nauthor Yahya Fakhroji <yahya.fakhroji@gmail.com> 1791288834 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791288834 +0700\n\nfix(search): Show why project search failed instead of \"No matches\" (#1639)\n\n**Problem**\nWhen the project search request failed, the search bar and the mobile\nsearch sheet treated it as an empty result and showed \"No matches in\nthis project.\" A 403 from the search API looked exactly like a project\nwith nothing in it, so users concluded their resources were missing.\n\n**Solution**\nBoth surfaces now check the engine''s error state before the\nempty-results branch and show an error message instead. A 403 reads\n\"Search isn''t available for your account in this project.\" The wording\nis neutral on purpose, because project owners currently hit this through\na missing backend grant. Any other failure reads \"Search is temporarily\nunavailable.\" The screen-reader status text uses the same copy. Unit\ntests cover the 403, 500 and empty-error cases.\n\nRefs #1619","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxOYCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyhMQAIbgsF+YPcfa5PINZLKtdCSQ\naQ/3NjIauZznf/Isjv+F0g5V2MzzzIVfBkvGoYMi44MjSlEkfFHKMqekESOIQBiW\n3cgszYnWWF7vgRhkYI1NaLkuECj5nvyAgYu9I43Gl19GHNADHi2NwMUWkVOTCnMC\nURpCjiK82AZZZV0Xm1W38ZwQ473pAZUFW8lUHW20mCcMCpPV/cD4Yg1FzMjgTUu8\nbvMjgN9lZLy1nLXoz6u1X/lQ5qzCIri5RcK7V3rZ1U73Y5Rftcppp+NqBpdiIw6l\nvCtrxF2m+lUyicO+8fWIAQSMYPpAV/PJIG/Bs8+i2bfF9FPpHsQrIgHVFiOtq/v4\nfUxoQ4xZ3u18G7hVRf86ueZ4hdVfFttYYDhOtIn8cY38UzzK/gf3o2rB+6CSjemw\n3MC3u+ml+oMevQppJqSmwAO0dtlLUNZhd32zsv+vz+VUZ6uwMHvtJCfaPxk93Tn/\nAJuHdfAIaUfPeDnG9stemmXGLRsn3OXsr70RLQaU/RG9RZ9gfK8JL8m05GeYD3J8\nIJ90cP7ygDXPx0Rlw0FX3c3g1e0D0tBB/Qt1nl/CZ0DJcbRFQseZKbSr2rySQMLN\nx3ZvVlMCVZytmcZApMb5mpgw81stfINMDivt39iNuVTL8v/B5SZhJdQ/pG7