1c25fe2bf9d75b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commits/524eb1046dec688231b66ce8261c25fe2bf9d75b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1724763?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kevwilliams","id":1724763,"login":"kevwilliams","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MjQ3NjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commits/3b1c97e0f6512a383a95bd4afcf37bc751fd8bc4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T21:30:14Z","email":"kwilliams@datum.net","name":"Kevin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T21:30:14Z","email":"kwilliams@datum.net","name":"Kevin"},"message":"perf: Compress portal responses at the gateway\n\nNothing between the browser and the portal compresses responses, so\nproduction ships its JS, CSS and HTML uncompressed (the largest chunk is\n1.8MB). Envoy''s default content types leave text/event-stream alone, so\nthe watch stream and assistant chat are unaffected.","tree":{"sha":"da02443a1b8df78cebc4737cb7619a61e68297be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/git/trees/da02443a1b8df78cebc4737cb7619a61e68297be"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/git/commits/3b1c97e0f6512a383a95bd4afcf37bc751fd8bc4","verification":{"payload":"tree da02443a1b8df78cebc4737cb7619a61e68297be\nparent d733c4c0e430ff07715ba5c4f2540487386fdd63\nauthor Kevin <kwilliams@datum.net> 1791235814 -0700\ncommitter Kevin <kwilliams@datum.net> 1791235814 -0700\n\nperf: Compress portal responses at the gateway\n\nNothing between the browser and the portal compresses responses, so\nproduction ships its JS, CSS and HTML uncompressed (the largest chunk is\n1.8MB). Envoy''s default content types leave text/event-stream alone, so\nthe watch stream and assistant chat are unaffected.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEEb8FNfGdgytwOrlKr53J8QGQJ2j0FAmrEFuYACgkQ53J8QGQJ\n2j2Bzw/9HCFOGqIiAYacXu/UesjaHBGhKn80f1rrHkcOgMH6OuE4J0biO1Www+eR\nEQlrZ6f7EJHE3rJ41lRp48esQCFgwwWgALTTh9WeUHGk+a8hod+zeQl1Bpr8eY5G\nXkDxwI7gSTkyrMJ3KvWMAnZdT7oNu8CtIZTPzjVsNw7s1Vjtoyt6OgNyvK8xQ9BX\n6qKiduBqCGvuo4+8BrPSe9wf7f6WidT+qGZaXhixDm2XCYkcLawgpkfb4ckGpMQb\nv+MsmD7oyF2jvKN4zMOxCgoTS7MarHV7hSosO9rAosYMosdPIzzwFoAGK/e/E8rL\nEsaYStXf14CT1iV44xqwhBQ9BZXvdCwq2+zVVTNu0mduvLtWUgBmLl6AlbfuU/6J\nr+4+Lr8UAx39Yd0m38gfWU8kStzpC922j0MYXOrPBnlTAGe3yxeyOQQQyILrU+kj\nzmFziQB+RJwtvTRm86CqSfwKTQBC6HTMJidoIsDnCkQOM9FeQVOyW0/L70QL9PLW\nTDMlQmroV/HcvrG8C7dYu9zRSTlsR69GBAPaArRhRpnuvBpbX6LmCAf9xp/5EjbC\nrZeEIpQFqw0l6J9ch2iIzs4H39NOYXSGaDYKEVKnAhfazmLFq5GnkiHk7vQz6O0a\neFfd6OOVEijtJzTqnonGmfIfuO+vN7RYB98xYDMpre71In+w1A4=\n=qk0h\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T21:30:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1724763?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kevwilliams","id":1724763,"login":"kevwilliams","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MjQ3NjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commit/3b1c97e0f6512a383a95bd4afcf37bc751fd8bc4","node_id":"C_kwDONzcdMtoAKDNiMWM5N2UwZjY1MTJhMzgzYTk1YmQ0YWZjZjM3YmM3NTFmZDhiYzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commit/d733c4c0e430ff07715ba5c4f2540487386fdd63","sha":"d733c4c0e430ff07715ba5c4f2540487386fdd63","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commits/d733c4c0e430ff07715ba5c4f2540487386fdd63"}],"sha":"3b1c97e0f6512a383a95bd4afcf37bc751fd8bc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commits/3b1c97e0f6512a383a95bd4afcf37bc751fd8bc4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75292329?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mattdjenkinson","id":75292329,"login":"mattdjenkinson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MjkyMzI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commits/d733c4c0e430ff07715ba5c4f2540487386fdd63/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T09:46:44Z","email":"75292329+mattdjenkinson@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Matt Jenkinson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T09:46:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Connect new ALBs to workloads, and stop pools pointing at one workload (#1629)\n\n**Problem**\n- An ALB with several backends still showed a \"View workload\" chip. It\nlinked to whichever workload published the ALB, which is only one\nbackend in the pool.\n- The \"No backend available\" headline came from the same label. Deleting\nthat one workload would have reported the whole pool as down, even with\nother backends still serving.\n- You could only point a new ALB at a public origin, even in projects\nwith compute.\n\n**Solution**\n\n*Pools on the overview*\n- The health strip no longer speaks for a single workload when there''s\nmore than one backend. It shows the \"N backends\" chip that URL pools\nalready use. Hovering it lists every backend with its share of traffic,\nor \"No traffic\" / \"Deleted\".\n- Each workload row on the Backends card links to that workload''s page.\n- Workloads that were deleted while the pool still references them get a\n\"Workload deleted\" chip, and their link is dropped.\n- The headline now judges a pool by its rows:\n- \"1 of 3 backends unavailable\", with a \"Manage backends\" chip, when\nsome workloads are gone.\n- \"No backend available\" only when nothing that receives traffic is\nleft.\n  - Backends with weight 0 don''t count.\n- Single-backend ALBs behave as before.\n\n<img width=\"930\" alt=\"Backend list tooltip on the 3 backends chip\"\nsrc=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/4eb52126f56ad8faf0f22ebcda7af73bae9be8ff/pool-backends-tooltip.png\"\n/>\n\n*Workload origins when creating an ALB*\n- In projects entitled to compute, Add an Application Load Balancer\noffers the same Public internet / Datum compute choice as Add backend.\nProjects without compute see the dialog as before.\n- Compute availability comes from `useComputePluginSlug`, the same check\nthe sidebar uses for Compute > Workloads.\n- The new ALB''s first backend is the workload''s NetworkService and the\nchosen port.\n- The ALB isn''t given the compute workload-name label. That label means\nthe workload''s deploys manage the ALB, and that deleting the workload\ndeletes it.\n- The origin cards and workload/port selects moved to\n`form/origin-type-fields.tsx`, shared by both dialogs.\n- Add backend now hides \"Datum compute\" in projects without compute.\nWhen you edit a backend that already points at a workload, the choice\nstays visible so you can still repoint it.\n\n<img width=\"430\" alt=\"Create ALB dialog with Datum compute selected\"\nsrc=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/4eb52126f56ad8faf0f22ebcda7af73bae9be8ff/create-alb-workload.png\"\n/>\n\n*Dependency*\n- `@datum-cloud/datum-ui` goes from 3.4.0 to 3.4.1. The patch only\nlightens badge borders.\n\n**Test plan**\n- [x] `bun run typecheck`, eslint, prettier\n- [x] `bun test app`: 1398 pass. New tests cover the per-row\ndeleted-workload state, the create payload for a workload origin, and\nschema validation for each origin type.\n- [x] Checked locally: create dialog with Datum compute, and the backend\ntooltip on a 3-backend pool (screenshots above)\n- [ ] Create an ALB from a workload and confirm it serves traffic\n- [ ] Delete one workload in a pool and check the headline and row chip","tree":{"sha":"25b49482e28583abd8f5d0fd1c02621d85dd5fb9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/git/trees/25b49482e28583abd8f5d0fd1c02621d85dd5fb9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/git/commits/d733c4c0e430ff07715ba5c4f2540487386fdd63","verification":{"payload":"tree 25b49482e28583abd8f5d0fd1c02621d85dd5fb9\nparent 1323cd41aecd0e04b9c89747fd61aabbfbd85765\nparent 3b95f866338a0fb559b2a84ac5edcd2b12a0c532\nauthor Matt Jenkinson <75292329+mattdjenkinson@users.noreply.github.com> 1791193604 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791193604 +0100\n\nConnect new ALBs to workloads, and stop pools pointing at one workload (#1629)\n\n**Problem**\n- An ALB with several backends still showed a \"View workload\" chip. It\nlinked to whichever workload published the ALB, which is only one\nbackend in the pool.\n- The \"No backend available\" headline came from the same label. Deleting\nthat one workload would have reported the whole pool as down, even with\nother backends still serving.\n- You could only point a new ALB at a public origin, even in projects\nwith compute.\n\n**Solution**\n\n*Pools on the overview*\n- The health strip no longer speaks for a single workload when there''s\nmore than one backend. It shows the \"N backends\" chip that URL pools\nalready use. Hovering it lists every backend with its share of traffic,\nor \"No traffic\" / \"Deleted\".\n- Each workload row on the Backends card links to that workload''s page.\n- Workloads that were deleted while the pool still references them get a\n\"Workload deleted\" chip, and their link is dropped.\n- The headline now judges a pool by its rows:\n- \"1 of 3 backends unavailable\", with a \"Manage backends\" chip, when\nsome workloads are gone.\n- \"No backend available\" only when nothing that receives traffic is\nleft.\n  - Backends with weight 0 don''t count.\n- Single-backend ALBs behave as before.\n\n<img width=\"930\" alt=\"Backend list tooltip on the 3 backends chip\"\nsrc=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/4eb52126f56ad8faf0f22ebcda7af73bae9be8ff/pool-backends-tooltip.png\"\n/>\n\n*Workload origins when creating an ALB*\n- In projects entitled to compute, Add an Application Load Balancer\noffers the same Public internet / Datum compute choice as Add backend.\nProjects without compute see the dialog as before.\n- Compute availability comes from `useComputePluginSlug`, the same check\nthe sidebar uses for Compute > Workloads.\n- The new ALB''s first backend is the workload''s NetworkService and the\nchosen port.\n- The ALB isn''t given the compute workload-name label. That label means\nthe workload''s deploys manage the ALB, and that deleting the workload\ndeletes it.\n- The origin cards and workload/port selects moved to\n`form/origin-type-fields.tsx`, shared by both dialogs.\n- Add backend now hides \"Datum compute\" in projects without compute.\nWhen you edit a backend that already points at a workload, the choice\nstays visible so you can still repoint it.\n\n<img width=\"430\" alt=\"Create ALB dialog with Datum compute selected\"\nsrc=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/4eb52126f56ad8faf0f22ebcda7af73bae9be8ff/create-alb-workload.png\"\n/>\n\n*Dependency*\n- `@datum-cloud/datum-ui` goes from 3.4.0 to 3.4.1. The patch only\nlightens badge borders.\n\n**Test plan**\n- [x] `bun run typecheck`, eslint, prettier\n- [x] `bun test app`: 1398 pass. New tests cover the per-row\ndeleted-workload state, the create payload for a workload origin, and\nschema validation for each origin type.\n- [x] Checked locally: create dialog with Datum compute, and the backend\ntooltip on a 3-backend pool (screenshots above)\n- [ ] Create an ALB from a workload and confirm it serves traffic\n- [ ] Delete one workload in a pool and check the headline and row chip","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw3IECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAt0YQACGR8aipd5FkurXdMHJolIv+\nSetAOLvqt8xkpC01RZcwFX7nudN//7fUnTF7sxJ4JcX/x7ZvIrVof8bY/O2kMdmP\nSLIWV5qSxzATc1SztOLMSlm6mHz3nDS29CjxXGlCLpJSMUnkNEa6d97IiFRAfAoy\n0cDh0dZh1j/Wd+/B10WhEqNup3bgqFhbS6rfopqp10S7KVHU/OQ67oBLbo5