tps://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commit/d0dcbb2c1a6bd3f4541eeb1b1d5c3439472b4a4f","node_id":"C_kwDONzcdMtoAKGQwZGNiYjJjMWE2YmQzZjQ1NDFlZWIxYjFkNWMzNDM5NDcyYjRhNGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commit/b9097b248b7bfeb8465a1e35f42c9d6a7eda4283","sha":"b9097b248b7bfeb8465a1e35f42c9d6a7eda4283","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commits/b9097b248b7bfeb8465a1e35f42c9d6a7eda4283"}],"sha":"d0dcbb2c1a6bd3f4541eeb1b1d5c3439472b4a4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commits/d0dcbb2c1a6bd3f4541eeb1b1d5c3439472b4a4f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75292329?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mattdjenkinson","id":75292329,"login":"mattdjenkinson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MjkyMzI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commits/b9097b248b7bfeb8465a1e35f42c9d6a7eda4283/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T11:53:32Z","email":"75292329+mattdjenkinson@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Matt Jenkinson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T11:53:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Upgrade @datum-cloud/datum-ui to 3.4 (#1613)\n\nUpgrades `@datum-cloud/datum-ui` to 3.4 in the portal and in the sample\nplugin.\n\n## Version jumps\n\n| Package | From | To |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Portal (`package.json`) | `^3.2.0` (3.2.0 locked) | `^3.4.0` (3.4.0) |\n| Sample plugin (`examples/sample-plugin/package.json`) | `^1.3.2`\n(1.4.0 locked) | `^3.4.0` (3.4.0) |\n\n### Portal: 3.2 → 3.4\n\n- **3.3** raised two peer floors: `js-yaml >=5.4.1`\n(GHSA-r3ph-w7gj-g6xm) and `@tiptap/* >=3.30.5` (ReDoS and\n`mergeAttributes` `__proto__` advisories). The lockfile already had\npatched versions (js-yaml 5.4.1, tiptap 3.31.3), so I only raised the\nranges in `package.json`: `js-yaml ^5.2.2 → ^5.4.1` and the seven\n`@tiptap/*` entries `^3.30.2 → ^3.30.5`. `@tiptap/pm` moves with the\nrest of the family. No resolved version changed.\n- **3.4** adds `orientation` and `onClose` to `AssistantWorkspace`. The\nportal doesn''t use `AssistantWorkspace`, so that part doesn''t affect it.\n3.4 also changes how `AppNavigation` behaves, and\n`app/layouts/dashboard.layout.tsx` uses it (see the visual checks\nbelow).\n\nThe portal needed no code changes.\n\n### Sample plugin: 1.x → 3.4\n\nThis crosses 2.0 (TanStack Table v9 and Motion v13 peers) and 3.0 (the\ntype-scale rename, and `Text`/`Title` colour inheritance). The sample\nonly imports `Badge`, `Button`, `Card`, `Separator` and `Skeleton`, so\nnone of the breaking changes touch it:\n\n| Migration | Files changed |\n| --- | --- |\n| `text-2xs` → `text-5xs`, then `text-1xs` → `text-2xs` | 0 (none used)\n|\n| `<Text size=\"base\">` → `size=\"sm\"` | 0 (no `Text`/`Title`/`Paragraph`)\n|\n| `Text`/`Title` colour inheritance | 0 |\n| `@tanstack/react-table` v9 / `motion` v13 | 0 (the sample depends on\nneither, and neither ends up in its lockfile) |\n| `EmptyContent` action API (1.0) | 0 (not used) |\n\nThe sample''s `Badge` and `Button` props (`type`, `theme`, `htmlType`,\n`size`) still typecheck against 3.4. Before this PR the sample built\nagainst 1.x types while the host served it 3.x components at runtime.\nNow both are on the same major.\n\nThe `shared` block in `vite.config.ts` stays as it is. It shares\n`badge`, `button`, `card`, `separator` and `skeleton`, which are exactly\nthe datum-ui subpaths the sample imports, and all of them are in the\nhost''s `DATUM_UI_SHARED`.\n\n**README (1 file):** The \"Shared singletons\" section in\n`examples/sample-plugin/README.md` was out of date. It said the host\nprovides exactly four singletons and told plugin authors not to share\ndatum-ui or the SDK. That contradicted both the sample''s own\n`vite.config.ts` and `federation-host.ts`. It now lists what the host\nactually shares, points to `DATUM_UI_SHARED`, and tells authors to keep\ntheir local datum-ui on the portal''s major. No datum-ui version numbers\nappear in the README or in `docs/enhancements/portal-plugin-system.md`.\n\n## Needs a visual check\n\n- **Sidebar (`AppNavigation`, 3.4 patch):** rows now stay the same\nheight whether the sidebar is collapsed or expanded. Group headers stay\nin the icon rail as a short rule and no longer get an active background\nwhen a child route is selected. Collapsing and expanding is now one\nmotion, with labels fading. Rail tooltips only open for a hover that\nstarts while the sidebar is collapsed. Check the project and org\nsidebars collapsed, expanded and hover-expanded.\n- **Sample plugin pages inside the portal:** they render with the host''s\ndatum-ui, which is already 3.x, so nothing should change. A quick look\nat Sample Plugin home, item detail, Platform data and the home card\nthrough `task plugin:preview` would confirm it.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `bun run typecheck` (root)\n- [x] `bunx eslint app/modules/plugins app/modules/project-nav\napp/layouts/dashboard.layout.tsx`: 0 problems (no TS files changed)\n- [x] `prettier --check` on the changed files\n- [x] `bun test app/modules/plugins`: 219 pass\n- [x] `bun test` (full suite): 1360 pass, 0 fail\n- [x] `bun run test:unit:prod` (Cypress component): 379 passing, 0\nfailing\n- [x] `bun run build` (production)\n- [x] Sample plugin: `bun run typecheck` and `bun run build`, with no\nwarnings\n- [ ] Visual check of the sidebar collapse, expand and hover-expand\nbehaviour\n- [ ] Visual check of the sample plugin pages loaded through the portal\n(`task plugin:preview`)","tree":{"sha":"563c787f055ecdc47943af15cd01be028d02831c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/git/trees/563c787f055ecdc47943af15cd01be028d02831c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/git/commits/b9097b248b7bfeb8465a1e35f42c9d6a7eda4283","verification":{"payload":"tree 563c787f055ecdc47943af15cd01be028d02831c\nparent 5779b2aa0d5b73c068ad7bf53430e6a68a437c5e\nparent 286eb7600445543d272c470d3a563913256846a8\nauthor Matt Jenkinson <75292329+mattdjenkinson@users.noreply.github.com> 1790855612 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790855612 +0100\n\nUpgrade @datum-cloud/datum-ui to 3.4 (#1613)\n\nUpgrades `@datum-cloud/datum-ui` to 3.4 in the portal and in the sample\nplugin.\n\n## Version jumps\n\n| Package | From | To |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Portal (`package.json`) | `^3.2.0` (3.2.0 locked) | `^3.4.0` (3.4.0) |\n| Sample plugin (`examples/sample-plugin/package.json`) | `^1.3.2`\n(1.4.0 locked) | `^3.4.0` (3.4.0) |\n\n### Portal: 3.2 → 3.4\n\n- **3.3** raised two peer floors: `js-yaml >=5.4.1`\n(GHSA-r3ph-w7gj-g6xm) and `@tiptap/* >=3.30.5` (ReDoS and\n`mergeAttributes` `__proto__` advisories). The lockfile already had\npatched versions (js-yaml 5.4.1, tiptap 3.31.3), so I only raised the\nranges in `package.json`: `js-yaml ^5.2.2 → ^5.4.1` and the seven\n`@tiptap/*` entries `^3.30.2 → ^3.30.5`. `@tiptap/pm` moves with the\nrest of the family. No resolved version changed.\n- **3.4** adds `orientation` and `onClose` to `AssistantWorkspace`. The\nportal doesn''t use `AssistantWorkspace`, so that part doesn''t affect it.\n3.4 also changes how `AppNavigation` behaves, and\n`app/layouts/dashboard.layout.tsx` uses it (see the visual checks\nbelow).\n\nThe portal needed no code changes.\n\n### Sample plugin: 1.x → 3.4\n\nThis crosses 2.0 (TanStack Table v9 and Motion v13 peers) and 3.0 (the\ntype-scale rename, and `Text`/`Title` colour inheritance). The sample\nonly imports `Badge`, `Button`, `Card`, `Separator` and `Skeleton`, so\nnone of the breaking changes touch it:\n\n| Migration | Files changed |\n| --- | --- |\n| `text-2xs` → `text-5xs`, then `text-1xs` → `text-2xs` | 0 (none used)\n|\n| `<Text size=\"base\">` → `size=\"sm\"` | 0 (no `Text`/`Title`/`Paragraph`)\n|\n| `Text`/`Title` colour inheritance | 0 |\n| `@tanstack/react-table` v9 / `motion` v13 | 0 (the sample depends on\nneither, and neither ends up in its lockfile) |\n| `EmptyContent` action API (1.0) | 0 (not used) |\n\nThe sample''s `Badge` and `Button` props (`type`, `theme`, `htmlType`,\n`size`) still typecheck against 3.4. Before this PR the sample built\nagainst 1.x types while the host served it 3.x components at runtime.\nNow both are on the same major.\n\nThe `shared` block in `vite.config.ts` stays as it is. It shares\n`badge`, `button`, `card`, `separator` and `skeleton`, which are exactly\nthe datum-ui subpaths the sample imports, and all of them are in the\nhost''s `DATUM_UI_SHARED`.\n\n**README (1 file):** The \"Shared singletons\" section in\n`examples/sample-plugin/README.md` was out of date. It said the host\nprovides exactly four singletons and told plugin authors not to share\ndatum-ui or the SDK. That contradicted both the sample''s own\n`vite.config.ts` and `federation-host.ts`. It now lists what the host\nactually shares, points to `DATUM_UI_SHARED`, and tells authors to keep\ntheir local datum-ui on the portal''s major. No datum-ui version numbers\nappear in the README or in `docs/enhancements/portal-plugin-system.md`.\n\n## Needs a visual check\n\n- **Sidebar (`AppNavigation`, 3.4 patch):** rows now stay the same\nheight whether the sidebar is collapsed or expanded. Group headers stay\nin the icon rail as a short rule and no longer get an active background\nwhen a child route is selected. Collapsing and expanding is now one\nmotion, with labels fading. Rail tooltips only open for a hover that\nstarts while the sidebar is collapsed. Check the project and org\nsidebars collapsed, expanded and hover-expanded.\n- **Sample plugin pages inside the portal:** they render with the host''s\ndatum-ui, which is already 3.x, so nothing should change. A quick look\nat Sample Plugin home, item detail, Platform data and the home card\nthrough `task plugin:preview` would confirm it.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `bun run typecheck` (root)\n- [x] `bunx eslint app/modules/plugins app/modules/project-nav\napp/layouts/dashboard.layout.tsx`: 0 problems (no TS files changed)\n- [x] `prettier --check` on the changed files\n- [x] `bun test app/modules/plugins`: 219 pass\n- [x] `bun test` (full suite): 1360 pass, 0 fail\n- [x] `bun run test:unit:prod` (Cypress component): 379 passing, 0\nfailing\n- [x] `bun run build` (production)\n- [x] Sample plugin: `bun run typecheck` and `bun run build`, with no\nwarnings\n- [ ] Visual check of the sidebar collapse, expand and hover-expand\nbehaviour\n- [ ] Visual check of the sample plugin pages loaded through the portal\n(`task plugin:preview`)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvkm8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZCgQADYmHlcnKlhQ7Cc9QKpl+eg0\nVehGpPJv14owgUS/BIjaOyAt0YOs7TMJCU444WKLh8NLbgLkA389eg75UryW472R\niZ18EEvir93MSDjGAn67MfA2B9NAgZrzcHgTXmcVmJ7jCytR+hagd37jCOe5vPuh\nsrfftM3QQPzmB+OXOIVafZfy5zl87v1ooLnftBZuAg3I