ved_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commit/286eb7600445543d272c470d3a563913256846a8","node_id":"C_kwDONzcdMtoAKDI4NmViNzYwMDQ0NTU0M2QyNzJjNDcwZDNhNTYzOTEzMjU2ODQ2YTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commit/5a0211db7e6c11742c12a5e5029a3d753e084617","sha":"5a0211db7e6c11742c12a5e5029a3d753e084617","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commits/5a0211db7e6c11742c12a5e5029a3d753e084617"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commit/5779b2aa0d5b73c068ad7bf53430e6a68a437c5e","sha":"5779b2aa0d5b73c068ad7bf53430e6a68a437c5e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commits/5779b2aa0d5b73c068ad7bf53430e6a68a437c5e"}],"sha":"286eb7600445543d272c470d3a563913256846a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commits/286eb7600445543d272c470d3a563913256846a8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75292329?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mattdjenkinson","id":75292329,"login":"mattdjenkinson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MjkyMzI5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commits/5779b2aa0d5b73c068ad7bf53430e6a68a437c5e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T11:45:55Z","email":"75292329+mattdjenkinson@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Matt Jenkinson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T11:45:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Let dock widgets render their own close button (#1612)\n\n**Problem**\nThe dock panel puts its close button on top of the widget''s top-right\ncorner. Patch''s chat now has a header with its own controls in that\ncorner (datum-ui 3.4''s vertical `AssistantWorkspace`), so the two\nbuttons sit on top of each other.\n\n**Solution**\nEvery `portal.dock/project` component is now mounted with an `onClose`\nprop. A widget that sets `handlesClose: true` in its manifest renders\nits own close control, and the panel then drops its overlay button.\nWidgets without the flag keep the overlay, so existing plugins are\nunaffected.\n\n- `DockProjectProperties.handlesClose` and `DockWidgetProps` are defined\nin `types.ts` and validated in the manifest schema.\n- `LazyPluginComponent` forwards optional `componentProps` to the plugin\ncomponent.\n- The dock''s loading skeleton now matches the chat''s vertical layout\n(top bar and empty state) rather than the old left rail.\n\n`DockWidgetProps` lives here for now. It belongs in\n`@datum-cloud/portal-plugin-sdk` eventually, so plugins can import the\ntype instead of copying it.\n\n**Rollout**\nMerge and deploy this before releasing the assistant plugin change that\nsets `handlesClose` (milo-os/assistant#113). An older portal ignores the\nflag and keeps its overlay button, which would then sit on top of the\nchat''s new-chat button.\n\nRelated: datum-cloud/datum-ui#228\n\n**Test plan**\n- [x] `bun run typecheck`, eslint, prettier\n- [x] `bun test app/modules/plugins`: 221 pass, including 2 new manifest\nschema tests (`handlesClose` accepted, non-boolean rejected)\n- [ ] With the updated assistant plugin: the dock shows a single close\nbutton (in the chat header), and it closes the panel\n- [ ] A dock widget without `handlesClose` still gets the overlay close\nbutton","tree":{"sha":"af7ad87bfef6ed7d7ce86e9923cb2296d4c67a74","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/git/trees/af7ad87bfef6ed7d7ce86e9923cb2296d4c67a74"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/git/commits/5779b2aa0d5b73c068ad7bf53430e6a68a437c5e","verification":{"payload":"tree af7ad87bfef6ed7d7ce86e9923cb2296d4c67a74\nparent 6ebcd09a542c87420c865e285c5ba897b0e52642\nparent 2b422e2e657fc3b5582778cf3fcef74ab9461942\nauthor Matt Jenkinson <75292329+mattdjenkinson@users.noreply.github.com> 1790855155 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790855155 +0100\n\nLet dock widgets render their own close button (#1612)\n\n**Problem**\nThe dock panel puts its close button on top of the widget''s top-right\ncorner. Patch''s chat now has a header with its own controls in that\ncorner (datum-ui 3.4''s vertical `AssistantWorkspace`), so the two\nbuttons sit on top of each other.\n\n**Solution**\nEvery `portal.dock/project` component is now mounted with an `onClose`\nprop. A widget that sets `handlesClose: true` in its manifest renders\nits own close control, and the panel then drops its overlay button.\nWidgets without the flag keep the overlay, so existing plugins are\nunaffected.\n\n- `DockProjectProperties.handlesClose` and `DockWidgetProps` are defined\nin `types.ts` and validated in the manifest schema.\n- `LazyPluginComponent` forwards optional `componentProps` to the plugin\ncomponent.\n- The dock''s loading skeleton now matches the chat''s vertical layout\n(top bar and empty state) rather than the old left rail.\n\n`DockWidgetProps` lives here for now. It belongs in\n`@datum-cloud/portal-plugin-sdk` eventually, so plugins can import the\ntype instead of copying it.\n\n**Rollout**\nMerge and deploy this before releasing the assistant plugin change that\nsets `handlesClose` (milo-os/assistant#113). An older portal ignores the\nflag and keeps its overlay button, which would then sit on top of the\nchat''s new-chat button.\n\nRelated: datum-cloud/datum-ui#228\n\n**Test plan**\n- [x] `bun run typecheck`, eslint, prettier\n- [x] `bun test app/modules/plugins`: 221 pass, including 2 new manifest\nschema tests (`handlesClose` accepted, non-boolean rejected)\n- [ ] With the updated assistant plugin: the dock shows a single close\nbutton (in the chat header), and it closes the panel\n- [ ] A dock widget without `handlesClose` still gets the overlay close\nbutton","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvkfzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGaEQACPvVrFS0xTcFo/IOfUb6uJH\nZIGsrCciaMqfsZ5RZNLP94nWDuHdaucO4wyOenz0zLXffOvfRGJlqvmSLhwEL1xw\nZGG2U4vqbN45riT1C/x+lGZZSTXSJUbyzt2D46mRgQgWPhwePZpHGChGuFqs13EP\nbjt4XXS/3/1Jxyo6ch8JSpQbQbx7AJQuJ2fzAzXyF48vqgOiWuccchv5TzZLU9Et\n3ox0f50rdpbFLVnESAAJDz+3DGEUZXb52wuJqwWu27kp775obMb35A8A8g5dtSWx\nh2OFvPahE4EokJxJ0AO+DWWOSC8zbyHSjJ1esn2uK4hWAzadjFqHdg4HuJ73+YnW\nmSBVGM/3wuqiTxW0Zk4+urwzRrEw6pCA7yZGR2KkC3T2vJ0e3F06C3nT6NFfWJAo\nE08a8J/esijCcD/4ZCAcAcRxGvUV4vi0LYtry7nGs4KUGgvU8rdgD5Id2QC9jQPT\nlPR6R2H5diLgIVGaZij/sY6s+4Qolkq7gknr8cD6TO5ElRYj0HfLweTUsL/RJ1gx\nDmD4pKthD1GXMF29v5EPoJopGFt+mzQi+A8Rmd8ERCnl9U9NZ+4aXY83fVibi1Xn\nT1dfEXIHqy5Im8LWJGvNrRS/LjUB3C/fUlbsyWVPsKymWi0EQhOiTuyKYFS476Xf\np/AmsanunZYggwcIJIW7\n=sD3P\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T11:45:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","follo