hubusercontent.com/u/6007097?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/scotwells","id":6007097,"login":"scotwells","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDcwOTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commits/c717f0a682048dbdec0171b28ff8d82440e9c5b9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T18:29:10Z","email":"wells.scot@gmail.com","name":"Scot Schuchert-Wells"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T18:29:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Let plugin pages open without the portal''s navigation (#1609)\n\nServices that open a page in its own browser window, like the instance\nshell in compute, had to show it with the portal''s sidebar and header\naround it, which filled most of a small window. A plugin page can now\nask for a bare layout, and the portal then renders only that page.\n\nThe page keeps its normal address and passes the same access checks and\ncontent security policy as any other plugin page.\n\nPortals without this change ignore the request and show the page with\nthe usual navigation, so plugins can adopt it before this ships. The\ncompute shell window in datum-cloud/compute#389 is the first user.\n\n## Design choice\n\nThe page''s own declaration picks the frame at its existing address,\nrather than a separate window route. That reuses the plugin loader\nuntouched, so a bare page can never skip a check, and a plugin opens one\nlink that works on every portal version.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Typecheck, lint and unit tests pass, including new cases for the\nmanifest field and for which page asks for the bare frame\n- [x] Against staging with the compute plugin loaded locally, the shell\nwindow shows only its title bar and terminal, with no sidebar, header or\ndock\n- [x] With the request removed from the plugin''s manifest, the same\nwindow renders inside the usual navigation and the terminal still fills\nit without scrolling\n- [x] Other plugin pages and the project home keep their navigation\n\nRelated to datum-cloud/enhancements#900","tree":{"sha":"afdcd3b56cb044b904f6028ff77c7f2d31636ac8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/git/trees/afdcd3b56cb044b904f6028ff77c7f2d31636ac8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/git/commits/c717f0a682048dbdec0171b28ff8d82440e9c5b9","verification":{"payload":"tree afdcd3b56cb044b904f6028ff77c7f2d31636ac8\nparent 3f8b2786d270682c94fedcba0d38c5acea9aaa83\nparent 072885f29889b872a34f028ce4085ac2a117c807\nauthor Scot Schuchert-Wells <wells.scot@gmail.com> 1790792950 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790792950 -0400\n\nfeat: Let plugin pages open without the portal''s navigation (#1609)\n\nServices that open a page in its own browser window, like the instance\nshell in compute, had to show it with the portal''s sidebar and header\naround it, which filled most of a small window. A plugin page can now\nask for a bare layout, and the portal then renders only that page.\n\nThe page keeps its normal address and passes the same access checks and\ncontent security policy as any other plugin page.\n\nPortals without this change ignore the request and show the page with\nthe usual navigation, so plugins can adopt it before this ships. The\ncompute shell window in datum-cloud/compute#389 is the first user.\n\n## Design choice\n\nThe page''s own declaration picks the frame at its existing address,\nrather than a separate window route. That reuses the plugin loader\nuntouched, so a bare page can never skip a check, and a plugin opens one\nlink that works on every portal version.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Typecheck, lint and unit tests pass, including new cases for the\nmanifest field and for which page asks for the bare frame\n- [x] Against staging with the compute plugin loaded locally, the shell\nwindow shows only its title bar and terminal, with no sidebar, header or\ndock\n- [x] With the request removed from the plugin''s manifest, the same\nwindow renders inside the usual navigation and the terminal still fills\nit without scrolling\n- [x] Other plugin pages and the project home keep their navigation\n\nRelated to datum-cloud/enhancements#900","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvVT2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZYYQAFOsaecA3G/k5mwLW2tgBf6t\n3DkPVVKJymth0WhmCpQV/b87vJIucQo3kBIjNouPH7Vq9LvurNiC6EcifE+fF6qZ\nX8638Luu1dQLW4m4x6vxKdCMxrC/wqKn9WGHabi4wsWBtqnMPJbgugh4TgKr6Xq/\nlAHf+nfDWOZMZZuSorajKS3dPkuFxXIjvOUQOfDovLZKJnB19hdRh4R2+dm7gY8z\nWK2pAVl7aCV6ClZh0vOipwVhtRGsU5l//p73tPTQUzEvIyuq04fXEk9r2QsIjA4e\nrqeo/ygMKwRKv1PXMPzi9JMIar3sll7AO/AW+W8pBeoUIREVgPHonBK5+qBsC8LW\nSlFBny51zUF+55FG2eTvcWMP5pH/vkn3WDKF1ln52jhFdvhPZQ5p5xmVMfw0yHql\ngPAKruVjcYKOeT8WuLyaMIRzrxZf4H6DWVePvWS0LCS2Tw21OS55RvSAg+7LJ/+h\nZBBKaIwlngKu/Lx5ySiqR8QFyQt2Y0GeJbuG9Qfjit+i0wtZ2ZNofKZGZ+wyUd0r\njSplD7IfBJhkqvDPCHHTkDz3cjkB1ycvkk6/bqWOD0Qz8w57v+YN+RNFZ04ZozXW\nvGWN0J8y3i1Hg7C6es/ldaRkBr8Oo55Bs9VZ2Q4enOPmJePjM8LRx2NBqTLqgIh4\nV6I50GEg4d1X7XQGXrsx\n=KFVS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T18:29:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commit/c717f0a682048dbdec0171b28ff8d82440e9c5b9","node_id":"C_kwDONzcdMtoAKGM3MTdmMGE2ODIwNDhkYmRlYzAxNzFiMjhmZjhkODI0NDBlOWM1Yjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commit/3f8b2786d270682c94fedcba0d38c5acea9aaa83","sha":"3f8b2786d270682c94fedcba0d38c5acea9aaa83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commits/3f8b2786d270682c94fedcba0d38c5acea9aaa83"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commit/072885f29889b872a34f028ce4085ac2a117c807","sha":"072885f29889b872a34f028ce4085ac2a117c807","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commits/072885f29889b872a34f028ce4085ac2a117c807"}],"sha":"c717f0a682048dbdec0171b28ff8d82440e9c5b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commits/c717f0a682048dbdec0171b28ff8d82440e9c5b9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1724763?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kevwilliams","id":1724763,"login":"kevwilliams","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MjQ3NjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commits/3f8b2786d270682c94fedcba0d38c5acea9aaa83/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T18:29:03Z","email":"kwilliams@datum.net","name":"Kevin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T18:29:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Turn the project home page into a launchpad (#1603)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe project home page only showed four onboarding cards, so once a\nproject was set up it had nothing left to offer.\n\nThe page now leads with a large project search, then a row of columns\nlisting the project''s domains, plugin-provided lists, and recently\nopened resources.\n\nPlugins add their own column through a new home column extension, and\nthe compute plugin''s Workloads column is the first to use it. Until a\nplugin provides one, a Workloads placeholder fills the slot.\n\n<img width=\"1241\" height=\"985\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b488ae69-06ec-46ad-a32b-46dbac89f53b\"\n/>\n\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b989edb4-81ff-4bae-8bbb-2007861952ae\n\n\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [ ] The home page shows search, Domains, the Workloads placeholder,\nand Recents, and the header search is hidden only on this page\n- [ ] Ctrl+K focuses the page search, and a resource opened from it\nappears in Recents\n- [ ] Domains lists up to five domains with status, and only users who\ncan create domains see Add domain\n- [ ] Unit tests, typecheck, and lint pass\n\nRelated to https://github.com/datum-cloud/compute/pull/386","tree":{"sha":"84e94e7a05645abcb22c84227ac98b0837668431","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/git/trees/84e94e7a05645abcb22c84227ac98b0837668431"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/git/commits/3f8b2786d270682c94fedcba0d38c5acea9aaa83","verification":{"payload":"tree 84e94e7a05645abcb22c84227ac98b0837668431\nparent aa0df3906469dab2607c7caeded8fc39f73db8e5\nparent f613dcf5382db92911804e7dd9b7a5f941bc7709\nauthor Kevin <kwilliams@datum.net> 1790792943 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790792943 -0700\n\nfeat: Turn the project home page into a launchpad (#1603)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe project home page only showed four onboarding cards, so once a\nproject was set up it had nothing left to offer.\n\nThe page now leads with a large project search, then a row of columns\nlisting the project''s domains, plugin-provided lists, and recently\nopened resources.\n\nPlugins add their own column through a new home column extension, and\nthe compute plugin''s Workloads column is the first to use it. Until a\nplugin provides one, a Workloads placeholder fills the slot.\n\n<img width=\"1241\" height=\"985\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b488ae69-06ec-46ad-a32b-46dbac89f53b\"\n/>\n\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b989edb4-81ff-4bae-8bbb-2007861952ae\n\n\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [ ] The home page shows search, Domains, the Workloads placeholder,\nand Recents, and the header search is hidden only on this page\n- [ ] Ctrl+K focuses the page search, and a resource opened from it\nappears in Recents\n- [ ] Domains lists up to five domains with status, and only users who\ncan create domains see Add domain\n- [ ] Unit tests, typecheck, and lint pass\n\nRelated to https://github.com/datum-cloud/compute/pull/386","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvVTvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2uQQAC9fIu7QMX1p50SgkrUck3Ny\nyWK1Fz7QfHacQx37O2U+u9r5P5siA9DXmFjqtIiqsHJvs14hqXsvXgnVbXj2E3dA\nNEaBPwtIknE3pQuFmKtXJyMpCPn5gucKIz9X+RFu+Vpgj81GOhnhnVS7ah+/oEPN\n8myPMTxe0xcy/4LcJwaESUdMzmmGkJ1xy+RY0o9BiklhsbxEfcKZOzXE0yCXNrvz\nLYIxEDPtYFVRehIWhkMcKVk7dcb5ySVII8vG6ofqnySo9sKYta8IRb0e2m51v5HH\nUR+7Y8qZee35lsnOZC4w6bg20hFt55jgegpjIYMhHwxkwoUFXC0dKISr5j/zqzvH\n6EZdarNsdGOmPXxOkW46qsNQjxj9Cmh2N1VO9wuUslAKtYBdWBH1trOgUCowj6xV\neqL9j48v+pyMsI0kBodYcQ5SoXJiHBLE7UFQCNUCBg5snoyHqeAUdHxoaQ7arECH\nZqKiyOlbNPuI4H8aVGlXZuFwSj+7FYKQfC1iYN8dDnx2zKWZRiPnZFRB1DbJcY8k\nDS4vluFDUbMlnRnLoh6/o3R64Ss3OxazTacU66IcpIoO75FXHRRt+Al59fIcz55t\ntx34DhJsaPdyL7Pzg8Qu/rncZgXK2W+maIYS7puKkeC8mu02fA2FCAWRJmQzn5OC\nW5c4h+hW4OQj2eRHi44u\n=Kc2l\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T18:29:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commit/3f8b2786d270682c94fedcba0d38c5acea9aaa83","node_id":"C_kwDONzcdMtoAKDNmOGIyNzg2ZDI3MDY4MmM5NGZlZGNiYTBkMzhjNWFjZWE5YWFhODM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commit/aa0df3906469dab2607c7caeded8fc39f73db8e5","sha":"aa0df3906469dab2607c7caeded8fc39f73db8e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commits/aa0df3906469dab2607c7caeded8fc39f73db8e5"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commit/f613dcf5382db92911804e7dd9b7a5f941bc7709","sha":"f613dcf5382db92911804e7dd9b7a5f941bc7709","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commits/f613dcf5382db92911804e7dd9b7a5f941bc7709"}],"sha":"3f8b2786d270682c94fedcba0d38c5acea9aaa83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commits/3f8b2786d270682c94fedcba0d38c5acea9aaa83"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6007097?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/scotwells","id":6007097,"login":"scotwells","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDcwOTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commits/072885f29889b872a34f028ce4085ac2a117c807/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T17:11:10Z","email":"wells.scot@gmail.com","name":"Scot Wells"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T17:11:10Z","email":"wells.scot@gmail.com","name":"Scot Wells"},"message":"feat: Let plugin pages render without the dashboard chrome\n\nA plugin that opens a page in its own browser window, such as the compute\nplugin''s instance shell, had no way to drop the portal''s sidebar, header and\ndock, so a small pop-up window spent most of its space on navigation.\n\nKey changes:\n- Add an optional `layout: \"bare\"` to `portal.page/project` extensions\n- Keep the same plugin URL and loader, so the registry, entitlement and\n  per-page RBAC checks and the CSP are unchanged; the loader reports whether\n  the page it gated is bare\n- Render a bare page with only the project and plugin-host providers around\n  it, skipping the navigation, header, dock, plugin nav fetches and the\n  last-used-project cookie\n- Portals that predate this ignore the field and show the page in the usual\n  chrome, so plugins can declare it before the portal ships","tree":{"sha":"a02423bd5c2c4bfed6a1e3199d9315e3784a9a0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/git/trees/a02423bd5c2c4bfed6a1e3199d9315e3784a9a0d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/git/commits/072885f29889b872a34f028ce4085ac2a117c807","verification":{"payload":"tree a02423bd5c2c4bfed6a1e3199d9315e3784a9a0d\nparent aa0df3906469dab2607c7caeded8fc39f73db8e5\nauthor Scot Wells <wells.scot@gmail.com> 1790788270 -0500\ncommitter Scot Wells <wells.scot@gmail.com> 1790788270 -0500\n\nfeat: Let plugin pages render without the dashboard chrome\n\nA plugin that opens a page in its own browser window, such as the compute\nplugin''s instance shell, had no way to drop the portal''s sidebar, header and\ndock, so a small pop-up window spent most of its space on navigation.\n\nKey changes:\n- Add an optional `layout: \"bare\"` to `portal.page/project` extensions\n- Keep the same plugin URL and loader, so the registry, entitlement and\n  per-page RBAC checks and the CSP are unchanged; the loader reports whether\n  the page it gated is bare\n- Render a bare page with only the project and plugin-host providers around\n  it, skipping the navigation, header, dock, plugin nav fetches and the\n  last-used-project cookie\n- Portals that predate this ignore the field and show the page in the usual\n  chrome, so plugins can declare it before the portal ships\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQR/ozPp/oJ2P+NplhUmONarzn3cYgUCar1CtQAKCRAmONarzn3c\nYhY2AP9SH+Is5L8207vRvuoLrVOfECnyI7zYFDjBg4bsYyKxYAEA/re3LeuqK8TY\nl6H4JSDWnBdIuiEJQWHZ+ngXOFvh1gw=\n=y2PE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T17:11:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6007097?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/scotwells","id":6007097,"login":"scotwells","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDcwOTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commit/072885f29889b872a34f028ce4085ac2a117c807","node_id":"C_kwDONzcdMtoAKDA3Mjg4NWYyOTg4OWI4NzJhMzRmMDI4Y2U0MDg1YWMyYTExN2M4MDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commit/aa0df3906469dab2607c7caeded8fc39f73db8e5","sh