ud/cloud-portal/commit/956e3e643d8f5e3fcf8dc74afd33b827ad0c0c0a","sha":"956e3e643d8f5e3fcf8dc74afd33b827ad0c0c0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commits/956e3e643d8f5e3fcf8dc74afd33b827ad0c0c0a"}],"sha":"0e3d8e2e3aae1615ee6342c124d74435c7062f9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commits/0e3d8e2e3aae1615ee6342c124d74435c7062f9c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6007097?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/scotwells","id":6007097,"login":"scotwells","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDcwOTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commits/956e3e643d8f5e3fcf8dc74afd33b827ad0c0c0a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T14:59:31Z","email":"wells.scot@gmail.com","name":"Scot Schuchert-Wells"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T14:59:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Let plugins declare allowlisted CSP additions (#1605)\n\nPlugins can now declare the few extra browser permissions they need, and\nthe portal checks each one against a strict allowlist before adding it\nto the page''s security policy. This unblocks the compute plugin''s\nin-browser instance shell, which runs a WebAssembly client in a\nbackground worker and connects to Datum''s relay servers. Nothing changes\nfor anyone else: with no declarations, the policy is byte-for-byte what\nit is today. Anything outside the allowlist is dropped and logged, never\napplied.\n\n## What changed\n\n- The existing (previously ignored) `contentSecurityPolicy` field on a\nplugin spec is now applied for every servable plugin, one `\"<directive>\n<source>...\"` entry each.\n- Only two additions are accepted: `script-src ''wasm-unsafe-eval''`, and\n`connect-src` with exact `https://` or `wss://` hostnames.\n- The field is added to the `ConsumerPortalPlugin` CRD so the API server\nstores it, and to `PORTAL_PLUGINS_JSON` for local development.\n- The security headers config moved into its own middleware; its output\nis unchanged when no plugin declares additions (verified against the\nprevious config in dev and production modes).\n\nExample declaration:\n\n```yaml\ncontentSecurityPolicy:\n  - \"script-src ''wasm-unsafe-eval''\"\n  - \"connect-src https://iroh-relay.us-central-1.datumconnect.net wss://iroh-relay.us-central-1.datumconnect.net\"\n```\n\n## Security reasoning\n\n- `''wasm-unsafe-eval''` permits compiling WebAssembly only. `eval()`,\n`new Function()` and inline script stay blocked, and the nonce plus\n`''strict-dynamic''` script policy is untouched, so the design''s \"never\n`unsafe-*`\" rule still holds for JavaScript. The design doc now names\nthis exception explicitly.\n- The portal is a single-page app with one policy per document, so\nadditions apply to every authenticated page, not only the plugin''s. Each\ndeclaration is a portal-wide trust decision made in service-catalog\nreview; the design doc and field docs say so. To keep that surface\nsmall, `connect-src` accepts exact hostnames only (no wildcards, ports,\npaths, `*`, `data:`, `blob:` or plaintext schemes).\n- `worker-src` is not allowlisted. An explicit value would stop the\nfallback to `script-src` on every page and block the `blob:` worker\nSentry Replay uses; the plugin''s same-origin worker already loads\nthrough that fallback.\n\nChecked in Chromium 149 against the real middleware, with a nonced page\nloading a plugin chunk that starts a same-origin worker, which runs\n`importScripts`, compiles WebAssembly and fetches a relay:\n\n| Policy | Plugin worker | Wasm (page and worker) | `eval` | Relay /\nother host | Sentry-style `blob:` worker |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Base | runs | blocked | blocked | blocked / blocked | runs |\n| With this PR''s additions | runs | works | blocked | allowed / blocked\n| runs |\n| Plus `worker-src ''self''` (rejected) | runs | works | blocked | allowed\n/ blocked | **blocked** |\n\nRelated: datum-cloud/compute#389 (shell tab), datum-cloud/compute#384\n(design).\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Unit tests: allowlisted additions applied, disallowed ones\n(including `worker-src`) rejected and logged, base policy unchanged,\nnonce present and fresh per request\n- [x] `bun test`, lint, typecheck and format all pass\n- [ ] Staging: the compute plugin declares the additions and the shell\nconnects with no CSP violations in the console\n- [ ] Staging: with no declarations, the page''s policy header matches\nproduction today\n\n\nRelated to datum-cloud/enhancements#900","tree":{"sha":"6d0d63652db7d6b7eddc0fa2ee4dd8144e024998","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/git/trees/6d0d63652db7d6b7eddc0fa2ee4dd8144e024998"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/git/commits/956e3e643d8f5e3fcf8dc74afd33b827ad0c0c0a","verification":{"payload":"tree 6d0d63652db7d6b7eddc0fa2ee4dd8144e024998\nparent f5c4c8f10706b027fffc0e6ce47b30eca53db316\nparent 40ca0b864442ace3bac4347ca8e9fca9f363182c\nauthor Scot Schuchert-Wells <wells.scot@gmail.com> 1790780371 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790780371 -0400\n\nLet plugins declare allowlisted CSP additions (#1605)\n\nPlugins can now declare the few extra browser permissions they need, and\nthe portal checks each one against a strict allowlist before adding it\nto the page''s security policy. This unblocks the compute plugin''s\nin-browser instance shell, which runs a WebAssembly client in a\nbackground worker and connects to Datum''s relay servers. Nothing changes\nfor anyone else: with no declarations, the policy is byte-for-byte what\nit is today. Anything outside the allowlist is dropped and logged, never\napplied.\n\n## What changed\n\n- The existing (previously ignored) `contentSecurityPolicy` field on a\nplugin spec is now applied for every servable plugin, one `\"<directive>\n<source>...\"` entry each.\n- Only two additions are accepted: `script-src ''wasm-unsafe-eval''`, and\n`connect-src` with exact `https://` or `wss://` hostnames.\n- The field is added to the `ConsumerPortalPlugin` CRD so the API server\nstores it, and to `PORTAL_PLUGINS_JSON` for local development.\n- The security headers config moved into its own middleware; its output\nis unchanged when no plugin declares additions (verified against the\nprevious config in dev and production modes).\n\nExample declaration:\n\n```yaml\ncontentSecurityPolicy:\n  - \"script-src ''wasm-unsafe-eval''\"\n  - \"connect-src https://iroh-relay.us-central-1.datumconnect.net wss://iroh-relay.us-central-1.datumconnect.net\"\n```\n\n## Security reasoning\n\n- `''wasm-unsafe-eval''` permits compiling WebAssembly only. `eval()`,\n`new Function()` and inline script stay blocked, and the nonce plus\n`''strict-dynamic''` script policy is untouched, so the design''s \"never\n`unsafe-*`\" rule still holds for JavaScript. The design doc now names\nthis exception explicitly.\n- The portal is a single-page app with one policy per document, so\nadditions apply to every authenticated page, not only the plugin''s. Each\ndeclaration is a portal-wide trust decision made in service-catalog\nreview; the design doc and field docs say so. To keep that surface\nsmall, `connect-src` accepts exact hostnames only (no wildcards, ports,\npaths, `*`, `data:`, `blob:` or plaintext schemes).\n- `worker-src` is not allowlisted. An explicit value would stop the\nfallback to `script-src` on every page and block the `blob:` worker\nSentry Replay uses; the plugin''s same-origin worker already loads\nthrough that fallback.\n\nChecked in Chromium 149 against the real middleware, with a nonced page\nloading a plugin chunk that starts a same-origin worker, which runs\n`importScripts`, compiles WebAssembly and fetches a relay:\n\n| Policy | Plugin worker | Wasm (page and worker) | `eval` | Relay /\nother host | Sentry-style `blob:` worker |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Base | runs | blocked | blocked | blocked / blocked | runs |\n| With this PR''s additions | runs | works | blocked | allowed / blocked\n| runs |\n| Plus `worker-src ''self''` (rejected) | runs | works | blocked | allowed\n/ blocked | **blocked** |\n\nRelated: datum-cloud/compute#389 (shell tab), datum-cloud/compute#384\n(design).\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Unit tests: allowlisted additions applied, disallowed ones\n(including `worker-src`) rejected and logged, base policy unchanged,\nnonce present and fresh per request\n- [x] `bun test`, lint, typecheck and format all pass\n- [ ] Staging: the compute plugin declares the additions and the shell\nconnects with no CSP violations in the console\n- [ ] Staging: with no declarations, the page''s policy header matches\nproduction today\n\n\nRelated to datum-cloud/enhancements#900","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvSPTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApdUQAIm4SMOij6TuCnvpB1OEg7Pu\nqp5IHTH192CAIjEMEpULB68V+xEjYNXcZ5nyyhvH7DjQurwvNM9GGGeAQwxQdEmp\nOT21LW61R0ZxFlcBFNzv1cshGtfo47OqnLijy5+wL0yQxesCBSi6r/4ivA2ztLeO\nbkLb8qecmsE72uyuHbbQo2BkiDuPOlFvOZojLmG/rBunIeE4gETwiVLq6hLTl+Pa\nF79Q+BsM2V8jgjXJcxxelg7bsKYmlNDqme3LF2QqobD4xep2KCnxvRVCqQNFL4zJ\nX/p0WHz9nT6Or/QuuUQ8To36YNYg4Rt6lLELc2uv+hQ8TXhPxlWp1nUpFZ/QbNh9\nPSMK7Ax7dKoTimcJKJIqaplehZ384MMqJ