ocument that plugin additions apply to the whole portal, so each one\n  is a portal-wide trust decision made in service-catalog review\n\nThe same check confirmed ''wasm-unsafe-eval'' lets WebAssembly compile in\nthe page and in the worker, while eval() and undeclared hosts stay\nblocked.","tree":{"sha":"6d0d63652db7d6b7eddc0fa2ee4dd8144e024998","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/git/trees/6d0d63652db7d6b7eddc0fa2ee4dd8144e024998"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/git/commits/40ca0b864442ace3bac4347ca8e9fca9f363182c","verification":{"payload":"tree 6d0d63652db7d6b7eddc0fa2ee4dd8144e024998\nparent 9a02ab1cd47b3e8860ac6c85ce7f63b7937ee6cd\nauthor Scot Wells <wells.scot@gmail.com> 1790730737 -0500\ncommitter Scot Wells <wells.scot@gmail.com> 1790777970 -0500\n\nfix: drop worker-src from plugin CSP allowlist\n\nAn explicit worker-src from any plugin would apply to every page and stop\nthe fallback to script-src, blocking the blob: worker Sentry Replay uses\nfor compression. Checked in Chromium 149: the plugin''s same-origin worker\nalready loads through the script-src fallback, so worker-src buys nothing.\n\nKey changes:\n- accept only script-src ''wasm-unsafe-eval'' and connect-src hosts\n- document that plugin additions apply to the whole portal, so each one\n  is a portal-wide trust decision made in service-catalog review\n\nThe same check confirmed ''wasm-unsafe-eval'' lets WebAssembly compile in\nthe page and in the worker, while eval() and undeclared hosts stay\nblocked.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQR/ozPp/oJ2P+NplhUmONarzn3cYgUCar0acgAKCRAmONarzn3c\nYvrlAQCLdUof8lOTUhw39JMCxKGTmOzsV+v+W+OH12FVhsphXgEA3uXpcY5VXCbG\nn5gT0dtb1aOudOV97/GzDTNIvRBOjQo=\n=xWr7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T14:21:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6007097?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sc