otwells/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/commits/9a02ab1cd47b3e8860ac6c85ce7f63b7937ee6cd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T23:57:13Z","email":"wells.scot@gmail.com","name":"Scot Wells"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T14:19:30Z","email":"wells.scot@gmail.com","name":"Scot Wells"},"message":"feat: apply allowlisted plugin CSP additions\n\nThe compute plugin''s instance shell runs a Go WebAssembly client in a\nWeb Worker that talks to iroh relays over HTTPS and WSS. The portal''s\npolicy blocks all three: no ''wasm-unsafe-eval'', no worker-src, and no\nrelay hosts in connect-src. Plugin specs already carry a\ncontentSecurityPolicy field, but it was parsed and never applied.\n\nKey changes:\n- merge contentSecurityPolicy entries from servable plugins into the\n  per-request policy, keeping the nonce and ''strict-dynamic'' intact\n- allow only script-src ''wasm-unsafe-eval'', worker-src ''self'', and\n  connect-src https:// or wss:// exact hostnames; reject and log the rest\n- add the field to the ConsumerPortalPlugin CRD so the API server stores\n  it, and to PORTAL_PLUGINS_JSON for local development\n- move the security headers config into its own middleware, unchanged\n  when no plugin declares additions\n\n''wasm-unsafe-eval'' permits WebAssembly compilation only; eval(),\nnew Function() and inline script stay blocked, so the design''s rule\nagainst unsafe-* script sources still holds for JavaScript.","tree":{"sha":"d9b70e0a74badcb9e51ddf96ee4e80587efb2cbf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/git/trees/d9b70e0a74badcb9e51ddf96ee4e80587efb2cbf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/cloud-portal/git/commits/9a02ab1cd47b3e8860ac6c85ce7f63b7937ee6cd","verification":{"payload":"tree d9b70e0a74badcb9e51ddf96ee4e80587efb2cbf\nparent f5c4c8f10706b027fffc0e6ce47b30eca53db316\nauthor Scot Wells <wells.scot@gmail.com> 1790726233 -0500\ncommitter Scot Wells <wells.scot@gmail.com> 1790777970 -0500\n\nfeat: apply allowlisted plugin CSP additions\n\nThe compute plugin''s instance shell runs a Go WebAssembly client in a\nWeb Worker that talks to iroh relays over HTTPS and WSS. The portal''s\npolicy blocks all three: no ''wasm-unsafe-eval'', no worker-src, and no\nrelay hosts in connect-src. Plugin specs already carry a\ncontentSecurityPolicy field, but it was parsed and never applied.\n\nKey changes:\n- merge contentSecurityPolicy entries from servable plugins into the\n  per-request policy, keeping the nonce and ''strict-dynamic'' intact\n- allow only script-src ''wasm-unsafe-eval'', worker-src ''self'', and\n  connect-src https:// or wss:// exact hostnames; reject and log the rest\n- add the field to the ConsumerPortalPlugin CRD so the API server stores\n  it, and to PORTAL_PLUGINS_JSON for local development\n- move the security headers config into its own middleware, unchanged\n  when no plugin declares additions\n\n''wasm-unsafe-eval'' permits WebAssembly compilation only; eval(),\nnew Function() and inline script stay blocked, so the design''s rule\nagainst unsafe-* script sources still holds for JavaScript.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQR/ozPp/oJ2P+NplhUmONarzn3cYgUCar0acgAKCRAmONarzn3c\nYvLKAQClTInO4QCB0SmMex0T8o0W62djtx5Z8rwAEwWYQGAEvwD/aoeUyu+6va0N\nUVa21elCoWKn8Es/zkAi+JyFfi+4XQI=\n=tx/D\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T14:21:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6007097?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.