,"type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rk4rohankumar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rk4rohankumar/pokemon-child-app/commits/f97a8a4fd149bf67cefcfb27cb90eafa8bc8d7dc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T04:35:17Z","email":"rwpmns@gmail.com","name":"Rohan Kumar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T04:35:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: shell-ready remote — singleton shared, async bootstrap, lazy media, a11y (#1)\n\n* feat: make the remote shell-ready (singleton shared, async bootstrap, lazy media, a11y)\n\nThe host shell loads this remote at runtime and initialises it with its own\nshare scope where react/react-dom are singletons. The old config shared\nreact/react-dom as `eager` (bundles a second React copy and breaks hooks\nwhen two instances meet), shared `tailwindcss` (a build-time tool, not a\nruntime module) and hard-coded the Vercel origin as publicPath, so the\nbuild only worked from that one URL.\n\n- craco: publicPath ''auto'' in production (dev keeps ''/''); share react,\n  react-dom, framer-motion and axios as singletons with requiredVersion\n  read from package.json; drop tailwindcss and eager.\n- src/index.js is now an async boundary (`import(''./bootstrap'')`) so the\n  shared modules are negotiated before App evaluates; bootstrap.js renders\n  under StrictMode and owns the index.css import.\n- Pokémon details are cached in memory by id and shared between pagination\n  and search, so paging back/forward or re-searching never refetches;\n  stale responses from superseded requests are ignored.\n- Sprites get explicit 475x475 dimensions; heading emoji is aria-hidden.\n- Type badges and the retry button now clear WCAG AA contrast (the only\n  Lighthouse a11y failure on the deployed site).\n- public/: real title/description/theme-color, inline SVG favicon, trimmed\n  manifest; CRA logos, favicon.ico, App.css, logo.svg, tests and\n  reportWebVitals removed (nothing referenced them).\n- README rewritten around what the host needs (scope, exposed module,\n  remoteEntry URL, singleton note).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(a11y): let the host own the main landmark\n\nThe exposed App rendered <main>, which nests a second main inside the\nshell''s. Root is now a labelled <section>; the standalone bootstrap adds\n<main> itself, matching the other remotes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6bab4c2d4344fccb59b77c3e4fa1e1c9f2d9cbef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rk4rohankumar/pokemon-child-app/git/trees/6bab4c2d4344fccb59b77c3e4fa1e1c9f2d9cbef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rk4rohankumar/pokemon-child-app/git/commits/f97a8a4fd149bf67cefcfb27cb90eafa8bc8d7dc","verification":{"payload":"tree 6bab4c2d4344fccb59b77c3e4fa1e1c9f2d9cbef\nparent a1493fb9faafeb7a9cfa89f1c7392eb8dc2c3746\nauthor Rohan Kumar <rwpmns@gmail.com> 1790915717 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790915717 +0530\n\nfeat: shell-ready remote — singleton shared, async bootstrap, lazy media, a11y (#1)\n\n* feat: make the remote shell-ready (singleton shared, async bootstrap, lazy media, a11y)\n\nThe host shell loads this remote at runtime and initialises it with its own\nshare scope where react/react-dom are singletons. The old config shared\nreact/react-dom as `eager` (bundles a second React copy and breaks hooks\nwhen two instances meet), shared `tailwindcss` (a build-time tool, not a\nruntime module) and hard-coded the Vercel origin as publicPath, so the\nbuild only worked from that one URL.\n\n- craco: publicPath ''auto'' in production (dev keeps ''/''); share react,\n  react-dom, framer-motion and axios as singletons with requiredVersion\n  read from package.json; drop tailwindcss and eager.\n- src/index.js is now an async boundary (`import(''./bootstrap'')`) so the\n  shared modules are negotiated before App evaluates; bootstrap.js renders\n  under StrictMode and owns the index.css import.\n- Pokémon details are cached in memory by id and shared between pagination\n  and search, so paging back/forward or re-searching never refetches;\n  stale responses from superseded requests are ignored.\n- Sprites get explicit 475x475 dimensions; heading emoji is aria-hidden.\n- Type badges and the retry button now clear WCAG AA contrast (the only\n  Lighthouse a11y failure on the deployed site).\n- public/: real title/description/theme-color, inline SVG favicon, trimmed\n  manifest; CRA logos, favicon.ico, App.css, logo.svg, tests and\n  reportWebVitals removed (nothing referenced them).\n- README rewritten around what the host needs (scope, exposed module,\n  remoteEntry URL, singleton note).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(a11y): let the host own the main landmark\n\nThe exposed App rendered <main>, which nests a second main inside the\nshell''s. Root is now a labelled <section>; the standalone bootstrap adds\n<main> itself, matching the other remotes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvzSFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA55AQAGYivVXH4dOlpfLzqsxWn9o6\nCfg/8rKN+DFPS/r8two4JatfKSswk+bvp8B5IE+JzRIdD9UIC905fPxRb1q6yLnZ\njezdgHUvVR5nE9i8v0ELXGd0IcywvLbqR/ROI7dzXC4wRx1xLqtLFMTUBXbHU666\nwhv0uyMB+4v7hp1Tj0lznAAKRLzekDpRnXfOBpuRXDNv7lvw9w+IHOgEWRjrHen/\n4YL0fzUpfG77sBSkZTG7os8t6A3XuIYUTGmUMKhZtj1yLO8W2szDhfBQFE7T/Iii\nPcno4o8DF/lToVAQVoEyrPC03xSvNk+2AU2VRQ76QaERpkP2mfej8Wjq6i76+MsW\n2PHu76gwc6WponjuAsf4TvjT67+JhzjGSSWE3ojSC5k/jDznrRc3/53TdQwiyy2y\nyO/BqJzEjVUfbmujoINKxQCtxGvSdg8/E57R5VVEGIliFVRhWmxv1VKf7dj7tKl2\n5Sv98z7JogGXoXhnex3P7UAkT65/9Z0ZIEl11j0V6KGqZsWy11zT2er68Dtk3vaX\nM6dtkMYLw3OIuCJfFEiJeXfojMH1VXeLnm3oDHAlJy49tYHezulu0gY3GHMJMYvo\nMzWhkxjzkhstImnqAxFpZ9ych195EZ9U9mPhXng7T7Gi8arh47/sJyLBS+2QwnpK\nQh0+U74xXA1Yra1yH1+5\n=t6J8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T04:35:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rk4rohankumar/pokemon-child-app/commit/f97a8a4fd149bf67cefcfb27cb90eafa8bc8d7dc","node_id":"C_kwDON0VIGNoAKGY5N2E4YTRmZDE0OWJmNjdjZWZjZmIyN2NiOTBlYWZhOGJjOGQ3ZGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rk4rohankumar/pokemon-child-app/commit/a1493fb9faafeb7a9cfa89f1c7392eb8dc2c3746","sha":"a1493fb9faafeb7a9cfa89f1c7392eb8dc2c3746","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rk4rohankumar/pokemon-child-app/commits/a1493fb9faafeb7a9cfa89f1c7392eb8dc2c3746"}],"sha":"f97a8a4fd149bf67cefcfb27cb90eafa8bc8d7dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rk4rohankumar/pokemon-child-app/commits/f97a8a4fd149bf67cefcfb27cb90eafa8bc8d7dc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96616262?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rk4rohankumar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rk4rohankumar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rk4rohankumar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rk4rohankumar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rk4rohankumar","id":96616262,"login":"rk4rohankumar","node_id":"U_kgDOBcI_Rg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rk4rohankumar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rk4rohankumar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rk4rohankumar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rk4rohankumar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rk4rohankumar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rk4rohankumar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rk4rohankumar/pokemon-child-app/commits/a1493fb9faafeb7a9cfa89f1c7392eb8dc2c3746/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-19T14:31:55Z","email":"rwpmns@gmail.com","name":"Rohan Kumar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-19T14:31:55Z","email":"rwpmns@gmail.com","name":"Rohan Kumar"},"message":"feat: perf + UX hardening\n\n- Paginate initial list (limit=20, offset), cache pages in memory — fixes N+1\n- Complete type-color map (all 18 types) in constants/\n- Debounced search with inline spinner\n- Show HP/Attack/Defense on cards, sprite fallback chain\n- Extract components (PokemonCard, Pagination, Error/Empty states)\n- Lazy images, prefers-reduced-motion, a11y landmarks\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5ba8a32c7e27afb365530437bb9e72b95e62926d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rk4rohankumar/pokemon-child-app/git/trees/5ba8a32c7e27afb365530437bb9e72b95e62926d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rk4rohankumar/pokemon-child-app/git/commits/a1493fb9faafeb7a9cfa89f1c7392eb8dc2c3746","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_