,"organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kinlane/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kinlane/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kinlane/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kinlane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kinlane/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kinlane","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/api-evangelist/ionic/commits/db1e96e222d2a14968178945db3d7b457409e244/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-02T14:35:35Z","email":"kinlane@gmail.com","name":"Kin Lane"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-02T14:35:35Z","email":"kinlane@gmail.com","name":"Kin Lane"},"message":"Kin Score 0.6 — provenance-graded rescore\n\nAdds this provider''s Kin Score artifact for rubric 0.6, the provenance release.\n\n0.6 grades on WHO PUBLISHED an artifact, not merely that one exists. Where API\nEvangelist authored an artifact on this provider''s behalf — a modeled OpenAPI, a\ncandidate MCP server, generated agent skills, a derived agentic-access contract —\nit now earns a quarter of the award rather than all of it. The artifact records\nthat authorship in its provenance block, so the number can be read with the\nevidence behind it.\n\nAlso in 0.6: contracts are scored in any format (OpenAPI, AsyncAPI, GraphQL SDL,\nFHIR CapabilityStatement); a spec whose servers[] resolve to a real host outscores\none declaring a placeholder or a bare template; idempotency, error semantics,\nrate-limit signalling and examples are read from the contract rather than from a\ndocumentation link; and no provider reaches Agent-Native without idempotency and a\nstable error envelope. Both band sets were re-cut against the new distribution.\n\nRubric: https://github.com/api-evangelist/kin-score","tree":{"sha":"ecafbae4afa7392bf463ae5ad0bb7334a8cacbe5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/api-evange