:05Z","email":"115213079+siriknikita@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Siryk Mykyta"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-05-03T12:10:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: Refactor docs build process with separate script and improved Mermaid loading (#39)\n\nThis pull request refactors the documentation build process by introducing a reusable template and a dedicated build script, improving maintainability and modularity. The most important changes include replacing inline build logic with a script, creating a standalone Docsify template, and updating the CI workflow to use the new script.\r\n\r\n### Documentation Build Process Refactor:\r\n\r\n* **Replaced inline build logic with `build-docs.sh`:** The documentation build process has been moved from the CI workflow file to a new shell script, `scripts/build-docs.sh`. This script handles directory creation, file copying, and template-based HTML generation.\r\n\r\n* **Introduced a reusable Docsify template:** A standalone Docsify HTML template (`docs/templates/docsify-template.html`) has been added. It includes improved Mermaid diagram handling, error styling, and a loading state for diagrams. This modular approach simplifies future updates to the Docsify configuration.\r\n\r\n* **Updated CI workflow to use the build script:** The `.github/workflows/docs.yml` file has been updated to replace the inline build logic with a call to the new `build-docs.sh` script, ensuring consistency and reducing duplication.","tree":{"sha":"decfcb30a2426a52594564b0d43e4a5a697f40ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/siriknikita/poly-micro-frontend-demo/git/trees/decfcb30a2426a52594564b0d43e4a5a697f40ad"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/siriknikita/poly-micro-frontend-demo/git/commits/53e15ad958c8b18124d8e9fe35c9f1f13b3ee33d","verification":{"payload":"tree decfcb30a2426a52594564b0d43e4a5a697f40ad\nparent 073d9c3981ecc51b66c41b3a5a77a932b3751bcc\nauthor Siryk Mykyta <115213079+siriknikita@user